{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel","id":842219,"title":"Claimed by an Angel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T16:15:57-08:00","id":842219,"title":"Claimed by an Angel","content":"It doesn't look like there's anything stopping an Angel from having the Claimed Manifestation ability. Demon doesn't exactly give any attention to the subject though, beyond providing the mechanics for it to be possible. I've never really looked into Werewolf or Spirits in first edition, which means that my knowledge of the Claimed is entirely based on the mechanics provided in the second edition books. So, I guess I'm mostly just looking for the other side of things, the fluff to accompany the mechanics. How would this play out? Why would the God-Machine design an Angel to Claim a human? What might such a creation look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:18:06-08:00","id":842220,"title":"","content":"The most likely situation is that the human is in some position that the GM needs to directly manipulate/oversee. So, say, the head of a major company or the leader of a major cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:24:42-08:00","id":842222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What might such a creation look like? </div> </div> </div>My first thought was <a href=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/--BNSHTFEU6Y/U0g0m0Ocq0I/AAAAAAAAtXk/SwWjQNtCYno/s1600/sus42.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://pre08.deviantart.net/050b/th/pre/i/2013/268/1/c/pope_bot_by_epscillion-d6nucdt.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> But either way, could do it to create &quot;blessed&quot; people who are the chosen of the god-machine disciples with the loyalty and powers of an angel with the ability to understand how humans think. Basically, away to have servants that ignore the God-Machines issue of having an alien intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:45:44-08:00","id":842356,"title":"","content":"This is a very interesting train of thought. I think Milo's hit it on the head, but I'lol go reread Preadators and get back to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T22:44:24-08:00","id":842416,"title":"","content":"On a related note, am I crazy or is there nothing that explicitly prevents an Angel from Claiming a Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:05:08-08:00","id":842422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=842416#post842416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, am I crazy or is there nothing that explicitly prevents an Angel from Claiming a Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does crazy awesome count? That's a really interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:19:50-08:00","id":842426,"title":"","content":"I don't remember, in 2E do Claimed directly add their stat dots to the host? If so, it could be an easy way to efficiently create much more capable servitors. Why build a Rank 2 Angel when you could build a Rank 1 to directly claim a human and get much the same direct efficiency, combined with an existing role within human society.<br /> <br /> Occult Matrixes can be based around specific individuals as well, perhaps the god machine can cheat what it means to be an individual by Claiming the subject directly, thus gaining much more control over the development of the Matrix.<br /> <br /> Another idea might be that certain angels can only &quot;incubate&quot; into a higher rank by first Claiming a host like a parasitic wasp larva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:21:46-08:00","id":842427,"title":"","content":"They do add their stat dots to the host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:34:30-08:00","id":842430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=842426#post842426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember, in 2E do Claimed directly add their stat dots to the host? If so, it could be an easy way to efficiently create much more capable servitors. Why build a Rank 2 Angel when you could build a Rank 1 to directly claim a human and get much the same direct efficiency, combined with an existing role within human society.<br /> <br /> Occult Matrixes can be based around specific individuals as well, perhaps the god machine can cheat what it means to be an individual by Claiming the subject directly, thus gaining much more control over the development of the Matrix.<br /> <br /> Another idea might be that certain angels can only &amp;quot;incubate&amp;quot; into a higher rank by first Claiming a host like a parasitic wasp larva.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossing Angels with Chestbusters sounds both horrific and awesome. That definitely will be a nasty surprise for a Demon or Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:44:08-08:00","id":842433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=842426#post842426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why build a Rank 2 Angel when you could build a Rank 1 to directly claim a human and get much the same direct efficiency, combined with an existing role within human society.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well for one, rank 1's cannot use Claim :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:56:50-08:00","id":842434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=842433#post842433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well for one, rank 1's cannot use Claim :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, the principle remains the same though, even if total efficiency is diminished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T18:10:04-08:00","id":842815,"title":"","content":"I can imagine a scenario where the G-M has a plan that simply can't be completed in a single human life-time, a plan that needs both angelic oversight and human sensibilities to be carried out adequately. The G-M chooses someone who already shows great charisma and understanding of the human mind to be Claimed by a powerful Angel (we're talking Rank 4 or 5 here). The resulting gestalt entity can pass off as a mortal, but possesses greatly increased capacities as well as supernatural powers. Mechanically, they'd be a Horror with Potency 6+ and Dread Powers meant to create and guide a very important Cult. Should this Cult leader be destroyed, the Angel flees and Claims another human, explaining it as a resurrection. Confronted with such power, the Cult would have renewed faith in their purpose, whatever it is. However, the subtle shifts in personality accumulated with each Claiming would lead one of the Cultists to ask inconvenient questions. Said conflicted Cultist might become an ally to a Ring of Demons investigating this plan, especially if the Cultist is a family member or friend of the main Cover of the Ring's leader.<br /> <br /> I know that's all vague. I'm not aiming for a full-fledged story seed, just an outline.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now that I think about it, this Angelic Cult could be in direct opposition to an Arisen Cult as part of the G-M's plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-05-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T18:36:43-08:00","id":842823,"title":"","content":"Now that's a very interesting idea. What I want to know is if said Angel Claimed would still retain the ability to use Incepts, and if they could develop Embeds as Dread Powers. It only makes sense- Demons lose Numina, gain Embeds and Exploits, so a Claimed Angel, who is also Ephemeral-turned-physical, should possess Embeds too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:28:30-08:00","id":844429,"title":"","content":"Bit of a nitpick, but a Rank 1 Angel <i>could</i> use Claim, if they swapped out two Numina for two additional Manifestations. It might not be very <i>good</i> at it unless it convinces the subject to go along with it or otherwise manages to negate their ability to resist, given its low dice-pool vs the contesting roll for even an average mortal (or monster), but it could certainly <i>try</i>.<br /> <br /> I'd think an Angel-Claimed would be able to use whatever Incepts the angel possessed, but given their inability to use Numina it'd be restricted to tweaking Influences and using the secondary ability each Incept grants. Unless you ruled that they could also apply to the Dread Powers that come with the package, that is, which could open all kinds of nasty new options. And if you ruled that Angel-Claimed could develop Embeds, as Arcanist suggested?<br /> <br /> On another note, I'd argue that, since Claiming melds two minds together, there's probably a lot of potential for triggering a Fall. Could make for an interesting story, actually. Though one wonders what might happen to the <i>host</i> should an angel Fall under this sort of circumstance...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:47:07-08:00","id":844434,"title":"","content":"You might end up with a more stable sort of Nephilim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:47:41-08:00","id":844436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bit of a nitpick, but a Rank 1 Angel <i>could</i> use Claim, if they swapped out two Numina for two additional Manifestations. It might not be very <i>good</i> at it unless it convinces the subject to go along with it or otherwise manages to negate their ability to resist, given its low dice-pool vs the contesting roll for even an average mortal (or monster), but it could certainly <i>try</i> </div> </div> </div>I thought you needed the right influences as well to get the conditions right.... might be misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:51:28-08:00","id":844437,"title":"","content":"That's just a shortcut. You never <i>need</i> influences to create any condition, there's always alternate methods given to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:59:10-08:00","id":844441,"title":"","content":"Quick glance at the Open Condition says that Influence is the <i>easiest</i> way to upgrade from Resonant/Anchor/Infrastructure (temporarily upgrading it as an instant action), so that's probably the most likely way to see Claiming happen by <i>far</i>. But the Condition also mentions acting in concert for a few scenes as a way of causing it, and Controlled (the direct requirement for someone being eligible for Claiming) stems from repeatedly Possessing a subject, which requires them to be Open. It'll take more time and effort without Influences speeding the process along, certainly, but it's mechanically possible right from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 03-09-2016, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T05:01:00-08:00","id":844442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=844429#post844429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of a nitpick, but a Rank 1 Angel <i>could</i> use Claim, if they swapped out two Numina for two additional Manifestations. It might not be very <i>good</i> at it unless it convinces the subject to go along with it or otherwise manages to negate their ability to resist, given its low dice-pool vs the contesting roll for even an average mortal (or monster), but it could certainly <i>try</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the God-Machine likely has a lot of willing cultists it could use if it wanted to efficiently manufacture a highly skilled specialist, as per Anachronistic Jam's original post. Pretty awesome thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T05:12:25-08:00","id":844445,"title":"","content":"That... is a valid point. From the perspective of a classic cultist, it'd sound like an offer to be blessed by... whatever they perceive the God-Machine as, and any personality changes they'd undergo could be hand-waved as &quot;being made aware of their divine purpose&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> It's kind of scary how well it actually fits, and despite the risk of one of its agents Falling due to the perspective shift, one has to wonder if it's maybe done somewhat regularly in the grand scheme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 03-09-2016, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:19:21-08:00","id":844586,"title":"","content":"Also, another Angel could be the one using Influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T21:02:56-08:00","id":844899,"title":"","content":"A loyal devotee visited by possibly multiple Angels, gifted with great divine power and purpose that they can't entirely grasp... suddenly, Angel-Claimed start sounding like prophets. Or if they're filled in a liiittle more and the Angel is particularly powerful, possibly even &quot;machine messiahs&quot;... wasn't there a thread a while ago based around the latter concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:04:38-08:00","id":845224,"title":"","content":"I think the one basic caution I'd offer is to consider why Angels most likely don't have the Claim Manifestation might have to do with the resource intensive nature of their creation. They're not just made casually, and a Claiming can mean losing the full Angel in favor of the hybrid. Rather than taking this as saying the God-Machine wouldn't do that, I'd urge you to try to consider the circumstances in which it would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:14:18-08:00","id":845231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845224#post845224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the one basic caution I'd offer is to consider why Angels most likely don't have the Claim Manifestation might have to do with the resource intensive nature of their creation. They're not just made casually, and a Claiming can mean losing the full Angel in favor of the hybrid. Rather than taking this as saying the God-Machine wouldn't do that, I'd urge you to try to consider the circumstances in which it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Claim is very specifically a thing you only see non-spirits using in weird edge cases \u2014 not for nothing is 1e's Claim Body only introduced as a ghost Numen in a Night Horrors book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:46:29-08:00","id":845284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845224#post845224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the one basic caution I'd offer is to consider why Angels most likely don't have the Claim Manifestation might have to do with the resource intensive nature of their creation. They're not just made casually, and a Claiming can mean losing the full Angel in favor of the hybrid. Rather than taking this as saying the God-Machine wouldn't do that, I'd urge you to try to consider the circumstances in which it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my entire question, yes. The books don't provide any information on the subject beyond &quot;This is a power Angels have, these are the mechanics&quot;. Hence this topic, asking people to pitch in with the story/fluff side of things.<br /> <br /> That said, there is a very, very obvious reason for why an Angel would have the Claim Manifestation ability. The God-Machine wishes to enact an Occult Matrix in which a Claimed human (or, more intriguingly, a Claimed Demon) is a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845231#post845231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Claim is very specifically a thing you only see non-spirits using in weird edge cases \u2014 not for nothing is 1e's Claim Body only introduced as a ghost Numen in a Night Horrors book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but feel 1E is entirely irrelevant, given that we're talking about a purely second edition game in which Claim is presented in the core book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:09:05-08:00","id":845297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845284#post845284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel 1E is entirely irrelevant, given that we're talking about a purely second edition game in which Claim is presented in the core book...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to your opinion, but seeing as the argument you're using is literally just &quot;it is technically possible to construct a character in this fashion&quot; and that same logic applies to stuff like &quot;I gave Host Jump to a spirit that doesn't have Possess, much less Claim,&quot; to say nothing of how the fundamentals of what ghosts are hasn't changed and literally none of the several example angels across Demon's entire run have Claim, I don't particularly care that you don't find a statement of precedent compelling evidence <i>that precedent exists along certain lines</i>.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine can and does use other ephemeral beings in its projects and it demonstrably doesn't need to commit an angel to the task of incorporating humans into its physical workings. This is very directly Weird Edge Case territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-10-2016, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:27:14-08:00","id":845316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845297#post845297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome to your opinion, but seeing as the argument you're using is literally just &quot;it is technically possible to construct a character in this fashion&quot; and that same logic applies to stuff like &quot;I gave Host Jump to a spirit that doesn't have Possess, much less Claim,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please, do me the courtesy of ditching the false equivalencies. An Angel with Claim can make use of it, else this topic would not exist. A Host Jumping being without the ability to Possess can not. The same logic does not apply, and it should be self evident why it does not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845297#post845297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to say nothing of how the fundamentals of what ghosts are hasn't changed and literally none of the several example angels across Demon's entire run have Claim, I don't particularly care that you don't find a statement of precedent compelling evidence <i>that precedent exists along certain lines</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the point about no existing Angels having Claim is a valid one. Perhaps only a totally convincing one if you only ever use example characters in your chronicles, but I can see where you're coming from with that angle and it's certainly easy to make the claim (heh) that Angels with this power would be rare.<br /> <br /> But that aside, the example you're talking about is for a species of Ephemeral Being unrelated to the topic at hand printed in a book published before Angels even <i>existed</i>. I'd be hesitant to credit Night Horrors as anything so valid as a &quot;precedent&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845297#post845297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine can and does use other ephemeral beings in its projects and it demonstrably doesn't need to commit an angel to the task of incorporating humans into its physical workings. This is very directly Weird Edge Case territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Satchel, there are no example Spirits with Claim in any of the Demon books working for the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> But enough jokes. Make my example an Occult Matrix that requires a being claimed by an Angel and it still works. So that's one Weird Edge Case. And again, the entire purpose of this topic was explicitly asking people for exactly those Weird Edge Cases. The books make this mechanically possible but don't discuss its practical application, so I'm asking the community for their ideas on when/why/how such an event would occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:30:49-08:00","id":845318,"title":"","content":"I think the answer that it might be required by an occult matrix is really the only situation I could conceive of. Otherwise, I'm inclined to agree that the God-Machine would <i>maybe </i>use someone Claimed by a spirit in some circumstances. Bonus points if it's an angel directing that effort.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the reason why it's worth looking at the 1E books is not because of some kind of legal precedent for the rules, but rather conceptual precedent. Looking at where certain mechanics were introduced in the original line helps you glimpse the intent of the writers, especially because they're working with the same (though perhaps updated) bibles that informed the writing of the 1e books.<br /> <br /> I think, insofar as Claiming is concerned, that we've seen it discussed in a few books. We've totally seen it talked about with regards to Spirits, a lot. Hell, Claimed are a central element of the antagonism between Spirits and Werewolves, and pretty much everywhere else they crop up (like in the Book of Spirits) it's also discussed.<br /> <br /> I think the difficulty I run into is that I can't really conceive of any situation besides an input for an occult matrix where Claiming somebody makes more sense than using a regular Angel or a servitor. <br /> <br /> To use another example of reading the books closely, we're informed repeatedly that the Machine likes to use existing infrastructure where possible. The way you can synthesize that and other behaviors is that it tries to accomplish its goals as efficiently as possible, using the least resources it can. Creating Angels requires an immense amount of resource, so the Machine is so averse to destroying them unless it has to that it's willing to send other Angels after Demons so it can recycle them into Angels again. We've seen a few instances of discussion where the God-Machine deliberately sets Angels against one another or to Fall and shit, but again it's almost always talked about in the context of occult matrices.<br /> <br /> So, what can be drawn from that is that it doesn't waste Angels unless they have to feed an occult matrix with their destruction/fall. It's got to be important to warrant that. Just the same, an angel Claiming somebody sounds like it's not likely to occur except for an occult matrix. So I'm not sure how many other edge cases can be manufactured.<br /> <br /> I guess as some advice/food for thought, I definitely think the coolest times this kind of Claimed thing should be used in an Occult Matrix would be ones that actually apply to Angels. Maybe this Claimed is the key input to create an even more powerful angel? Or to make something like the Galatea hook in <i>Splintered City: Seattle</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-10-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:49:47-08:00","id":845328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845316#post845316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh please, do me the courtesy of ditching the false equivalencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You first. Angels aren't spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, the point about no existing Angels having Claim is a valid one. Perhaps only a totally convincing one if you only ever use example characters in your chronicles, but I can see where you're coming from with that angle and it's certainly easy to make the claim (heh) that Angels with this power would be rare. </div> </div> </div>It's a power that has, in the entire printed run of 1e and 2e alike, only ever actually shown up in the stat blocks of spirits and a scant handful of strange ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that aside, the example you're talking about is for a species of Ephemeral Being unrelated to the topic at hand printed in a book published before Angels even <i>existed</i>. </div> </div> </div>Again, as the only other sort of example of an ephemeral being with the ability to claim when even prior to the textual introduction of angels there were at least three such categories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd be hesitant to credit Night Horrors as anything so valid as a &quot;precedent&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Your decision to claim the invalidity of a subline that currently has one of its books listed as reference material in its corresponding 2e corebook is your own. Your decision to discount a subline <i>devoted to weird edges cases</i> when asking about the construction of a weird edge case is also your own.<br /> <br /> Your decision to try to call me out on providing a supporting statement not addressed to you is further your own and is presently contributing very little to your pursuit aside from dragging in a decidedly pointless argument on a subject whose answer is pretty much literally &quot;this is strange and rare enough to not have established precedent beyond the most basic 'do as you need for your story.'&quot;<br /> <br /> You've gotten enough answers that you can afford to not aggravate an aside like this. Leave me be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T16:42:38-08:00","id":845347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845318#post845318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the answer that it might be required by an occult matrix is really the only situation I could conceive of. Otherwise, I'm inclined to agree that the God-Machine would <i>maybe </i>use someone Claimed by a spirit in some circumstances. Bonus points if it's an angel directing that effort.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the reason why it's worth looking at the 1E books is not because of some kind of legal precedent for the rules, but rather conceptual precedent. Looking at where certain mechanics were introduced in the original line helps you glimpse the intent of the writers, especially because they're working with the same (though perhaps updated) bibles that informed the writing of the 1e books.<br /> <br /> I think, insofar as Claiming is concerned, that we've seen it discussed in a few books. We've totally seen it talked about with regards to Spirits, a lot. Hell, Claimed are a central element of the antagonism between Spirits and Werewolves, and pretty much everywhere else they crop up (like in the Book of Spirits) it's also discussed.<br /> <br /> I think the difficulty I run into is that I can't really conceive of any situation besides an input for an occult matrix where Claiming somebody makes more sense than using a regular Angel or a servitor.<br /> <br /> To use another example of reading the books closely, we're informed repeatedly that the Machine likes to use existing infrastructure where possible. The way you can synthesize that and other behaviors is that it tries to accomplish its goals as efficiently as possible, using the least resources it can. Creating Angels requires an immense amount of resource, so the Machine is so averse to destroying them unless it has to that it's willing to send other Angels after Demons so it can recycle them into Angels again. We've seen a few instances of discussion where the God-Machine deliberately sets Angels against one another or to Fall and shit, but again it's almost always talked about in the context of occult matrices.<br /> <br /> So, what can be drawn from that is that it doesn't waste Angels unless they have to feed an occult matrix with their destruction/fall. It's got to be important to warrant that. Just the same, an angel Claiming somebody sounds like it's not likely to occur except for an occult matrix. So I'm not sure how many other edge cases can be manufactured.<br /> <br /> I guess as some advice/food for thought, I definitely think the coolest times this kind of Claimed thing should be used in an Occult Matrix would be ones that actually apply to Angels. Maybe this Claimed is the key input to create an even more powerful angel? Or to make something like the Galatea hook in <i>Splintered City: Seattle</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, tangentially, that Claiming is a Big Deal for Spirits and Werewolves. Which is sort of why it became a topic of interest to me. If it's so significant, why is it available for Angels with no word count dedicated to its impact on the setting? Spirit-only effects exist are called out as such and Claimed is not one of them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the obvious conclusion, which I was able to come to on my own, was that the writers didn't really see Angels Claiming people as a big enough deal to talk about. Nevertheless it's an option and given how integral it is to Werewolf it can clearly lead to some interesting stories. Hence this topic.<br /> <br /> Now, personally, I feel there are a few more options than just &quot;Occult Matrices&quot; as an explanation for why the God-Machine may seek to manifest an Angel with the Claimed Manifestation. But first of all:<br /> <br /> Why, exactly, is this seen as &quot;wasting an angel&quot;? The Angel still exists. If its body is destroyed, it can move on and Claim a new target. It loses access to Numen, sure, but it still <i>exists</i>, it can still contribute to future projects, it can still follow the God-Machine's orders and use its Influences and has a new unique skill set unlike many of its angelic siblings with which to carry it out. It can even abandon its Claimed body if its Ephemeral form becomes more useful to the God-Machine's next mission. So why this idea that dedicating an Angel to Claiming a target is equivalent to destroying the Angel?<br /> <br /> In terms of reasons to Claim, the obvious ones that leap out are:<br /> <br /> -Infiltration. The Angel can access the target's mind, and <i>be</i> the target in every way once it has been Claimed. Obviously, this works best when the Claimed Being is one whose physical alterations can be discreetly concealed. In Demon, certain changes could be passed off as glitches/partial transformations.<br /> -Motivation. Getting a Saboteur to give up all their secrets is a whole lot easier if they become a loyal Angel, merging their personalities so that at least part of them wants to help.<br /> -Special skill sets. The Claimed being can develop Supernatural Merits. These can be combined with the Angel's influences to create abilities that Ephemeral Angels couldn't possibly possess. Combined with the massively boosted attributes and long term nature of Claimed, this could be a lot more useful to a variety of projects than a Possessed or Materialised Angel.<br /> -Efficiency. At least in terms of Essence. I mean, it's certainly clear that the God-Machine has no trouble producing Essence, but as it strives to reach results in the most efficient manner it could be that a being able to operate without Essence for prolonged periods of time could be attractive for it due to the corresponding reduction in supply costs.<br /> -&quot;God moves in mysterious ways&quot;. Yeah, this is really just the Occult Matrix argument, but a little broader. No one understands occult physics. Maybe the Machine only had the resources to manufacture an Angel with the Claimed ability. Maybe there would have been unacceptable side effects to specialising the Angel in a different direction. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:01:38-08:00","id":845355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware, tangentially, that Claiming is a Big Deal for Spirits and Werewolves. Which is sort of why it became a topic of interest to me. If it's so significant, why is it available for Angels with no word count dedicated to its impact on the setting? Spirit-only effects exist are called out as such and Claimed is not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because it isn't Spirit-only, but rather, a thing that mostly Spirits do. The ghosts or angels that would do it are the kind of one-off edge cases you'd see in a Night Horrors book (which incidentally, is one of the reason's why Satchel's post is a valuable one to think about.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, the obvious conclusion, which I was able to come to on my own, was that the writers didn't really see Angels Claiming people as a big enough deal to talk about. Nevertheless it's an option and given how integral it is to Werewolf it can clearly lead to some interesting stories. Hence this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the conclusion to draw is that it's not a big deal, but rather that it is sufficiently <i>uncommon </i>that dedicating wordcount outside of detailing that edge-case in the <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>core was not considered worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, personally, I feel there are a few more options than just &quot;Occult Matrices&quot; as an explanation for why the God-Machine may seek to manifest an Angel with the Claimed Manifestation. But first of all:<br /> <br /> Why, exactly, is this seen as &quot;wasting an angel&quot;? The Angel still exists. If its body is destroyed, it can move on and Claim a new target. It loses access to Numen, sure, but it still <i>exists</i>, it can still contribute to future projects, it can still follow the God-Machine's orders and use its Influences and has a new unique skill set unlike many of its angelic siblings with which to carry it out. It can even abandon its Claimed body if its Ephemeral form becomes more useful to the God-Machine's next mission. So why this idea that dedicating an Angel to Claiming a target is equivalent to destroying the Angel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mistakenly misremembered Claiming as permanently merging the two, such that an Angel no longer exists. That was my mistake.<br /> <br /> In terms of reasons to Claim, the obvious ones that leap out are:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Infiltration. The Angel can access the target's mind, and <i>be</i> the target in every way once it has been Claimed. Obviously, this works best when the Claimed Being is one whose physical alterations can be discreetly concealed. In Demon, certain changes could be passed off as glitches/partial transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that the God-Machine follows the path of least resistance:<br /> <br /> 1. Claiming as it's described in the <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>core has an effect on the body. Passing them off as glitches doesn't really make sense, since a glitch is in and of itself an attention-grabbing thing.<br /> 2. If it needs to know something you know, it can send an Angel or a Stigmatic or an Imperative that's capable of reading your mind as a mundane mortal, which is certainly less intrusive and noticeable (also things the God-Machine prefers)<br /> 3. Concealment Infrastructure is already purpose-made for this sort of thing. Sleeper Agents, Places that take people's lives and turn them into Covers, all that stuff can do the deed without the time and resource investment of manufacturing an Angel to Claim a person just to infiltrate something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Motivation. Getting a Saboteur to give up all their secrets is a whole lot easier if they become a loyal Angel, merging their personalities so that at least part of them wants to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the above. If the Machine wants to know that Demon's secrets, there's ways that are less time consuming and resource intensive than Claiming him. In fact, I'd bet good money it'd use Infrastructure to recycle him and get his memories. Don't forget that Claiming takes a long period of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Special skill sets. The Claimed being can develop Supernatural Merits. These can be combined with the Angel's influences to create abilities that Ephemeral Angels couldn't possibly possess. Combined with the massively boosted attributes and long term nature of Claimed, this could be a lot more useful to a variety of projects than a Possessed or Materialised Angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stigmatics provide these talents in a less resource intensive fashion, since again, you don't have to make an Angel to do it. In fact, this is why Stigmatics are called out as valuable to the Machine, because they don't even represent the smallest fraction of the cost of an Angel.<br /> <br /> Angelic Incepts provide a means of boosting the scale of power for abilities they possess that seems again (in an ironic twist) to be less resource intensive/time consuming than making somebody Claimed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Efficiency. At least in terms of Essence. I mean, it's certainly clear that the God-Machine has no trouble producing Essence, but as it strives to reach results in the most efficient manner it could be that a being able to operate without Essence for prolonged periods of time could be attractive for it due to the corresponding reduction in supply costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just fail to see how a Claimed is more efficient than the already existing purpose-built Infrastructure, Angels, Stigmatics and Incepts that cover all of the aforementioned purposes. I'm not saying that it's completely inferior to every iteration of the above, but at a glance, Claiming seems the least efficient way to accomplish these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-&quot;God moves in mysterious ways&quot;. Yeah, this is really just the Occult Matrix argument, but a little broader. No one understands occult physics. Maybe the Machine only had the resources to manufacture an Angel with the Claimed ability. Maybe there would have been unacceptable side effects to specialising the Angel in a different direction. Who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's completely fair.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the record, I'm not at all opposed to an Angel with Claimed. I definitely think it's a very interesting idea, but I don't feel that these explanations provide a good rationale for why the Machine would do it outside of very specific Occult Matrix edge-cases.<br /> <br /> Your last reason, while similar to the occult matrix explanation is IMHO the most compelling, because the question of &quot;Why would the Machine make an angel to merge with a person?&quot; is more compelling when the answer is not something as mundane and (generally) incorrect like &quot;It's more efficient.&quot;<br /> <br /> As another suggested thought, I think when considering what weird reason the Machine may have to send an Angel to Claim somebody that the human part of that should be very important. It's not made this Angel to Claim just any schmuck, this person is important to the Machine's plans. But how? Why? What was their disposition <i>BEFORE </i>the Angel Claimed them? What are they like now? Perhaps most interestingly, how might that interact with the potential for an Angel to Fall?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:13:44-08:00","id":845360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845347#post845347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, exactly, is this seen as &quot;wasting an angel&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Claiming a living being \u2014 especially something with as much potential for occult entanglement as a human \u2014 is a synthesis that neither component comes away from without picking up bits of the other even after separation. Arc's made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217778-inspiration-from-demon?p=218544#post218544\">at least one fairly extensive essay</a> talking about how the God-Machine and its errant tools are very much built on the notion of being <i>apart</i>. You're looking at the Manifestation as an abstraction that's neater than the practical execution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So why this idea that dedicating an Angel to Claiming a target is equivalent to destroying the Angel? </div> </div> </div>Regular interaction with humanity is already enough to cause a distressing number of angels to Fall off-schedule and the purely mechanical effects of Claiming are available to the Machine without blowing the esoteric equivalent of hundreds to billions of dollars. Weird bio-psychic engineering can give a mortal supernatural powers that aren't thematically derived from the nature of a given angel and a slavish devotion to a given agenda that isn't vulnerable to the sudden development of independence, and Bunyip's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804918-homebrew-g-m-numina?p=815001#post815001\">mentioned</a> that angels in Cover essentially shortcut away the entire Manifestation system.<br /> <br /> Unless there's a <i>specific call</i> for such a risk, God has tools at Its disposal that can do most all of the jobs a Claimed might be called upon for without outright merging an angel with a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-10-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:34:56-08:00","id":845369,"title":"","content":"Claim can be used against supernatural targets, right? Could it be that Angels Claim when they need access to a supernatural creatures and manipulation is, for whatever reason, not an option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:38:31-08:00","id":845372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845328#post845328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You first. Angels aren't spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never once did I call an Angel a Spirit. Giving an Angel Claim does not equate it to a Spirit at all. There are Spirit-only manifestation effects on the very table that lists Claim. Claim is not one of them. It sounds like your prior readings have led you to the idea that Spirits are the only ones who Claim. That's fine as a personal view, but as per the second edition books it's wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845328#post845328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a power that has, in the entire printed run of 1e and 2e alike, only ever actually shown up in the stat blocks of spirits and a scant handful of strange ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is a totally true statement. As I mentioned, the lack of space dedicated to discussing the idea is why this topic was made.<br /> <br /> Of course, Angels didn't exist in first edition, so it not showing up on them there is not exactly surprising.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845328#post845328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, as the only other sort of example of an ephemeral being with the ability to claim when even prior to the textual introduction of angels there were at least three such categories.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now Angels are the third category. And the core book now lists it as valid for Ghosts, Spirits, and Angels alike. In first edition it only listed it for Spirits and Ghosts, but Angels didn't exist. That doesn't strike me as particularly damning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845328#post845328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your decision to claim the invalidity of a subline that currently has one of its books listed as reference material in its corresponding 2e corebook is your own. Your decision to discount a subline <i>devoted to weird edges cases</i> when asking about the construction of a weird edge case is also your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrespective of its subject matter, it doesn't come off as a supplement addressing the topic of Angels and <i>anything</i> if it was written before Angels were a thing. But whatever, agree to disagree I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845328#post845328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your decision to try to call me out on providing a supporting statement not addressed to you is further your own and is presently contributing very little to your pursuit aside from dragging in a decidedly pointless argument on a subject whose answer is pretty much literally &quot;this is strange and rare enough to not have established precedent beyond the most basic 'do as you need for your story.'&quot;<br /> <br /> You've gotten enough answers that you can afford to not aggravate an aside like this. Leave me be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mate, I'm not personally attacking you or calling you out. I addressed Leetespeak's post as well in the post you're talking about, you were hardly singled out. I'm sorry if you felt the post should not have been responded to.<br /> <br /> However, I don't feel this discussion is even close to pointless. I enjoy this kind of forum debate, at times for its own sake but more importantly for things like my previous post addressing Leetespeak. In the course of that post a number of ideas coalesced in terms of the purpose and usefulness of the Claim Manifestation that I had not previously consciously thought of. Leetespeak's own post was in response to our discussion on the validity of a 1E book. That means that this argument has already provided creative thought that I can use in my games. The point has never been to attack you, or even convince you that you're wrong (which I don't even think you are in terms of &quot;Claiming is a thing Angels don't do very often&quot;, I'm just quibbling over some of your reasoning). The point is to get something creative out of it. That's the point of these entire forums. And shutting down the topic because we're talking about something strange and rare seems ludicrous. We have the books for the common scenarios, and the community for exactly this kind of discussion.<br /> <br /> If you're unhappy with the discussion, by all means leave. I find this kind of discussion useful for getting my own thoughts in order, critically examining where I am coming from, and even mining opposing arguments for ideas to use in game. That's useful enough to me that I fully intend to respond to just about every post in this topic where I feel I have something to say. Although, of course, this particular part of this post is getting off topic, so we can probably forego continuing this particular element of debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T17:58:41-08:00","id":845377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845372#post845372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never once did I call an Angel a Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are treating the fact that Manifestations exist in a common pool as though it were an indication that there are no meaningful distinctions between the behavior and tendencies of the two &quot;species.&quot; Spirits do not exist in Twilight under the same set of assumptions as angels do, and their reliance on Manifestations takes an accordingly different tenor than the divine executors who only need to worry about being consumed during inactivity in exceptional circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Giving an Angel Claim does not equate it to a Spirit at all. There are Spirit-only manifestation effects on the very table that lists Claim. Claim is not one of them. </div> </div> </div>I did all the time I cared to do in the &quot;But It Doesn't Say!&quot; Argument mines back on the old forums in 2010. The book also doesn't give a Rank limit to Possess, but we've got word from the guy who wrote the system that you typically won't find a ghost with it that hasn't spent some time in the Underworld (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/113788-ghosts-and-possession?p=113914#post113914\">it's essentially what skinriders are in the 2e paradigm</a>). The lack of hard mechanics for a trend does not equate to its nonexistence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounds like your prior readings have led you to the idea that Spirits are the only ones who Claim. </div> </div> </div>Reading the first post I made in this topic should make the absurdity of this assumption clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And shutting down the topic because we're talking about something strange and rare seems ludicrous. We have the books for the common scenarios, and the community for exactly this kind of discussion. </div> </div> </div>Which is why quibbling with someone's agreement that this particular scenario is significantly uncommon is a waste of time that could be better spent on, say, making example situations that can serve an actual use instead of equivocating about the abstract implications of power formatting.<br /> <br /> Leet's mentioned the prospect of Claiming as part of the mechanism of summoning a more powerful angel, for instance; what might the occult matrix need to do with the resulting hybrid during and after the output is achieved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-10-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T18:37:07-08:00","id":845385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, because it isn't Spirit-only, but rather, a thing that mostly Spirits do. The ghosts or angels that would do it are the kind of one-off edge cases you'd see in a Night Horrors book (which incidentally, is one of the reason's why Satchel's post is a valuable one to think about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not much that can practically be gleaned from &quot;this doesn't happen very often&quot;. If you're going to use it in a game, talking about the where/why/how of when it does occur is more useful than talking about all the instances where it doesn't happen. Even if the evidence were more than tangential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the conclusion to draw is that it's not a big deal, but rather that it is sufficiently <i>uncommon </i>that dedicating wordcount outside of detailing that edge-case in the <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>core was not considered worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Could have been that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mistakenly misremembered Claiming as permanently merging the two, such that an Angel no longer exists. That was my mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, no worries. I was rereading my copy of the book wondering if I'd missed something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind that the God-Machine follows the path of least resistance:<br /> <br /> 1. Claiming as it's described in the <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>core has an effect on the body. Passing them off as glitches doesn't really make sense, since a glitch is in and of itself an attention-grabbing thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean more in the scenario in which the Demons you are trying to infiltrate look in askance and go &quot;Why is your left arm sweating gasoline?&quot; you can at least claim it's a sign of your Demon-ness rather than being exposed as an Angel.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If it needs to know something you know, it can send an Angel or a Stigmatic or an Imperative that's capable of reading your mind as a mundane mortal, which is certainly less intrusive and noticeable (also things the God-Machine prefers)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind-reading flat out wouldn't work on a Demon.<br /> <br /> ...it's up in the air whether it would work on a Claimed Demon, for sure. That's definitely something we could discuss in this topic. If an Angel Claims a Demon and they become one, can the Demon spoof the Claiming Angel's ability to examine its thoughts? Lots of weird things feel like they could happen from there.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Concealment Infrastructure is already purpose-made for this sort of thing. Sleeper Agents, Places that take people's lives and turn them into Covers, all that stuff can do the deed without the time and resource investment of manufacturing an Angel to Claim a person just to infiltrate something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the thing, of course. They may have security measures that a Sleeper without some supernatural tolerance could not be expected to pass, for example. Or they might, you know, read the mind of the agent you send in and if it's not the person they were expecting (the one you previously Claimed) then you might be in trouble. A Claimed being can have a pretty broad skill-set thanks to access to Incepts and Influences, and be capable of doing more damage on their own than a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the above. If the Machine wants to know that Demon's secrets, there's ways that are less time consuming and resource intensive than Claiming him. In fact, I'd bet good money it'd use Infrastructure to recycle him and get his memories. Don't forget that Claiming takes a long period of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know that recycling a Demon actually gives access to its memories? Sure, specific Infrastructure for that purpose could be created, but it's a coin flip as to whether that would take any less effort to summoning an Angel and an Angel with the ability to Claim could even <i>be</i> that Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stigmatics provide these talents in a less resource intensive fashion, since again, you don't have to make an Angel to do it. In fact, this is why Stigmatics are called out as valuable to the Machine, because they don't even represent the smallest fraction of the cost of an Angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Stigmatic will have much smaller dice pools, and may or may not develop the precise powers the God-Machine is looking for. They're cheaper, but they're undeniably going to be worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angelic Incepts provide a means of boosting the scale of power for abilities they possess that seems again (in an ironic twist) to be less resource intensive/time consuming than making somebody Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claimed could do both, since the power doesn't make mention of an Angel losing its Incepts when it Claims.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just fail to see how a Claimed is more efficient than the already existing purpose-built Infrastructure, Angels, Stigmatics and Incepts that cover all of the aforementioned purposes. I'm not saying that it's completely inferior to every iteration of the above, but at a glance, Claiming seems the least efficient way to accomplish these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think a long range scout. The God-Machine has Infrastructure most places, but no everywhere. There are places in the world where Saboteurs have freed locations from Infrastructure. There are other Dimensions largely untouched. An Angel will eventually run out of Essence due to Essence Bleed and a lack of favourable Conditions. A Claimed being could operate in these circumstances more or less indefinitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I'm not at all opposed to an Angel with Claimed. I definitely think it's a very interesting idea, but I don't feel that these explanations provide a good rationale for why the Machine would do it outside of very specific Occult Matrix edge-cases.<br /> <br /> Your last reason, while similar to the occult matrix explanation is IMHO the most compelling, because the question of &quot;Why would the Machine make an angel to merge with a person?&quot; is more compelling when the answer is not something as mundane and (generally) incorrect like &quot;It's more efficient.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree. Which, again, is the kind of thing I've been asking for in this thread. That kind of brainstorming of circumstances and scenarios is exactly what the books lack and what I'm asking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845355#post845355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another suggested thought, I think when considering what weird reason the Machine may have to send an Angel to Claim somebody that the human part of that should be very important. It's not made this Angel to Claim just any schmuck, this person is important to the Machine's plans. But how? Why? What was their disposition <i>BEFORE </i>the Angel Claimed them? What are they like now? Perhaps most interestingly, how might that interact with the potential for an Angel to Fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the person would take on the Angel's Virtue and Vice is actually really interesting, especially given how weird an Angel's Virtue and Vice could be. If the God-Machine needs to make that specific alteration, Claiming is definitely one way to achieve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T18:38:56-08:00","id":845386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845377#post845377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to clarify, you are ok if I respond to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:23:48-08:00","id":845413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845386#post845386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to clarify, you are ok if I respond to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to stick to the last sentence and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811828#post811828\">not equate the Unchained with the Fallen</a>, then sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:49:28-08:00","id":845424,"title":"","content":"For the record, while there's nothing saying you can't, having an angel Claim is pretty out of place within the reasoning and aesthetic of God-machine/Demon stories. I mean, if Claiming were an easy answer, why bother with Messengers or their ilk when dealing with humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:02:31-08:00","id":845435,"title":"","content":"Demon's Storyteller Guide offers this line, 'Angels in the Spiral World also retain the ability to fetter, unfetter, possess and claim people and objects as they would normally.' I'm unsure if my copy is the most up-to-date version but it does imply that it happens.<br /> <br /> I think of Claiming to be a last-resort sort of option, though. It seems like the sort of thing that would lead to increased chances of falling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:11:00-08:00","id":845436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=845424#post845424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, while there's nothing saying you can't, having an angel Claim is pretty out of place within the reasoning and aesthetic of God-machine/Demon stories. I mean, if Claiming were an easy answer, why bother with Messengers or their ilk when dealing with humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>That just reinforces for me that the GM would use it when not dealing with humans. The Matrix requires a vampire of exact specifications, or even better a Beast that can tell that the Angel is not kin... That's when possession and claiming start to look more attractive. It's still a very fringe case, buts cases like that which end up making good stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:31:08-08:00","id":845443,"title":"","content":"The response to that is so deep and varied I can't even do it justice tonight. So let's go reader's digest here: the angels must be careful about maintaining the purity of their being, which is simultaneously their body, their soul, and their active mind, their thoughts. Claiming <i>anything</i> is to introduce the sort of unclean, unholy deviance to their exist that can cause them to Fall. On the flip side, descending(ba dum ching) to the same level as most living things via Claiming is an affront to the celestial authority and awesome power that is the sphere of the angels-it diminishes them, makes them appear less credible, less <i>absolute</i>. So Falling aside, it just weakens the message any angels conveys.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that claiming doesn't happen. It just has to happen for the right reasons, and in such a way that conveys the particular brand of sacred presence that the God-Machine cultivates, both in the angels themselves and those who come across them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:44:48-08:00","id":845454,"title":"","content":"While I doubt that its what you wanted to inspire Arc, that just leaves me with the image of a cleansing angel in my mind, that purifies monsters be Claiming them. Of course, he who fights monsters and all that... I think you could pull something like that off if you worked it correctly, which I think you and I both agree on. Its just a matter of finding the right balance and recognizing how rare it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:52:02-08:00","id":845459,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it can happen. I wouldn't say you couldn't do it. The toolbox allows for it in ways that most people's ideas just couldn't. Far be it from me to say no when the game doesn't even have to flinch to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Just, you know, it's something you <i>think</i> about doing <i>before</i> you do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:30:09-07:00","id":849899,"title":"","content":"So let's say this is possible. Can a Angel who claimed a body Fall? And if so, what happens to the body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:41:42-07:00","id":849904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/842219-claimed-by-an-angel?p=849899#post849899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's say this is possible. Can a Angel who claimed a body Fall? And if so, what happens to the body?</div> </div> </div> </div> That depends on whether or not the Angel is also carrying out another mission that requires a more typical Cover instead of Claiming. The Claimed human probably doesn't count as a Cover, so if the Angel does Fall while they are fused, I assume the body of the human is destroyed or damaged beyond repair. The Angel either reaches for its genuine Cover, or is Burned until they create one. However, pieces of the human's mind/soul might linger within the Demon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T15:56:29-07:00","id":849911,"title":"","content":"For simplicity's sake, I'd argue that they can't Fall while the Claiming is active (but after separation is fair game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}